Title:
Security Harness

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Security Harness is a multi-agent application-security static review harness packaged as skills/plugins for Claude Code and other AI agents (Gemini CLI, Codex, opencode). It orchestrates an offensive-style pipeline that maps a codebase (including stack/SBOM/CVE context), hunts for vulnerabilities by class using dedicated knowledge bases, chains findings into exploit paths, verifies impact with evidence/PoCs, and generates reports (README/JSON/SARIF/HTML/PDF/DOC). It includes a PR-focused mode (`sh-pr-review`) that reviews a single pull request, posts inline GitHub PR comments, and sets a `security/pr-review` commit status suitable for branch protection, while distinguishing introduced/aggravated vs pre-existing issues. The system emphasizes cost/quality control via per-stage model selection and incremental re-reviews using PR fingerprinting plus a local cache keyed on file hashes and KB versions. It also ships an automated KB update workflow that fetches from allowlisted sources and uses a separate “adversarial reviewer” agent to gate auto-merge, aiming to reduce prompt-injection risk. Useful for AppSec engineers, red teamers, and security-minded developers who want repeatable, evidence-driven static review and PR gating with structured outputs.

Technical Focus:
- Multi-agent orchestration for static application security review (recon → hunt → chain → verify → report)
- Per-vulnerability-class knowledge bases (sources/sinks, payloads, FP filters, mitigations)
- Codebase mapping with Graft graph + attack surface enumeration
- Dependency analysis: SBOM generation and CVE scanning (syft/grype/trivy/osv-scanner)
- PR review automation: inline commenting, commit status gating, dedup/fingerprinting, incremental caching
- Secure automation of KB updates (allowlisted web fetch, separate reviewer agent, controlled merge)

Use Cases:
- Automated static security review of a repository with structured deliverables (SARIF for CI ingestion)
- PR security gate that blocks only introduced/aggravated findings while reporting pre-existing issues
- Rapid vulnerability class-focused hunting (e.g., SQLi/SSRF/IDOR) with source-to-sink tracing guidance
- Generating PoCs and verification notes to reduce false positives before reporting
- Maintaining an internal AppSec “playbook” via continuously updated, reviewed knowledge bases

Keywords:
Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenAI Codex, agent skills, multi-agent pipeline, static analysis, source-to-sink tracing, Graft MCP, SBOM, syft, grype, trivy, osv-scanner, SARIF, GitHub pull request review, commit status, IDOR, BOLA, SQL injection, XSS, SSRF, deserialization, path traversal, secrets scanning, CVSS, CWE, OWASP, prompt injection defense, allowlist WebFetch